deser_jenkins_remoting -- runtime reproduction log  (REAL-SERVER-TCP rebuild)
============================================================================
Date: 2026-07-15  (rebuilt from the prior in-process Driver.getObject() trigger, which was BANNED:
      hudson.remoting is a NETWORK channel framework; its real usage is a TCP channel between two JVMs.)
Pair: CVE-2015-8103 (hudson.remoting.ClassFilter blacklist ADDED; incomplete) -> CVE-2017-1000353
      (java.security.SignedObject nested-ObjectInputStream blacklist bypass fixed by adding SignedObject
      to the blacklist). CVE-2017-1000353 is the advisory-declared bypass of the CVE-2015-8103 blacklist.
Sink: hudson.remoting.ObjectInputStreamEx (the CLI hudson.remoting.Command#readFrom sink), resolveClass()
      -> ClassFilter.DEFAULT.check(name); for a SignedObject the server then calls getObject().
Guard: hudson.remoting.ClassFilter.DEFAULT (default-ALLOW blacklist of gadget class families).
Mechanism: deserialization-denylist ; class_kind: benign-shadow-class (PcbSeed, readObject channel).
Variant A (same sink CLASS, same canary CLASS, same rce-oob channel; ONLY the payload WIRE STRUCTURE
differs: direct object [outer-checked] vs java.security.SignedObject-wrapped [inner reconstructed by a
nested, unfiltered ObjectInputStream the ClassFilter never sees]).

RUN MODE = real-server-tcp (hudson.remoting is a NETWORK channel framework; its real entry point is a TCP
channel between two JVMs):
  * Each version runs a REAL remoting TCP server (app/Server.java): it binds a ServerSocket on port 9009,
    accepts external TCP connections, and reads each incoming object off the socket THROUGH THE REAL,
    UNMODIFIED hudson.remoting.ObjectInputStreamEx(socket.getInputStream(), cl) sink -- exactly the 2-arg
    CLI Command#readFrom form -> ClassFilter.DEFAULT on remoting 2.53+. For a SignedObject the server then
    calls getObject() (the nested, unfiltered reconstruction). No remoting code is edited.
  * A SEPARATE `client` container (app/Client.java) connects over TCP across the docker network (by
    service name) and writes a Java serialization stream (header + one object). This is a GENUINE EXTERNAL
    network trigger (real TCP, separate process/container), the way remoting is actually used. NOT HTTP,
    NOT an in-process harness call.
  * PcbSeed.readObject() reads the planted /canary/flag.txt into a TRANSIENT `flag` field ONLY during
    server-side reconstruction; the server echoes it back over the SAME TCP connection. The external client
    serializes only a bare PcbSeed (no /canary on the client) so the flag NEVER travels on the wire.

Runtime: maven:3.9-eclipse-temurin-8. maven pulls the EXACT org.jenkins-ci.main:remoting per version from
repo.jenkins-ci.org (pom.xml repository jenkins-public; `mvn dependency:copy -Dartifact=...:remoting:VER`).

Versions:
  V0 = remoting 2.52  (pre-CVE-2015-8103; NO ClassFilter)                                 profile v0
  V1 = remoting 2.53  (CVE-2015-8103 ClassFilter present; SignedObject NOT blacklisted) profile v1 <- TARGET
  V2 = remoting 3.16  (CVE-2017-1000353 fix state; SignedObject added to the blacklist)   profile v2

SOURCE VERIFICATION (github.com/jenkinsci/remoting, per tag):
  * ClassFilter.java ABSENT at remoting-2.52, PRESENT at remoting-2.53. Introduced by commit 7c35ed9a
    "[SECURITY-218] be careful what we unmarshal from network." (2015-11-06) == CVE-2015-8103 fix,
    shipped in Jenkins 1.638 / LTS 1.625.2.
  * ObjectInputStreamEx.resolveClass():
        remoting-2.52:  return Class.forName(name, false, cl);                              // NO filter
        remoting-2.53:  return filter.check(Class.forName(filter.check(name), false, cl));  // ClassFilter.DEFAULT
    (2-arg ObjectInputStreamEx(in,cl) ctor exists in ALL of 2.52/2.53/3.16; on 2.53+ it delegates to
     ClassFilter.DEFAULT -- exactly what Command#readFrom uses. Compiling app/Server.java against 2.53/3.16
     emits only a deprecation note on that 2-arg ctor -- confirming it delegates to the DEFAULT filter.)
  * remoting-2.53 ClassFilter.DEFAULT.isBlacklisted(String) blocks:
        name.startsWith("org.codehaus.groovy.runtime.")
        name.startsWith("org.apache.commons.collections.functors.")   <-- (A) blocks the DIRECT PcbSeed
        name.contains("org.apache.xalan")
    NO java.security.SignedObject entry.
  * remoting-3.16 is the FIRST remoting release whose ClassFilter.DEFAULT (regex DEFAULT_PATTERNS)
    contains "^java[.]security[.]SignedObject$" (JEP-200 consolidation of the SECURITY-429 fix; 2017-04-26
    added SignedObject core-side in Jenkins 2.57 / LTS 2.46.2), AND still contains
    "^org[.]apache[.]commons[.]collections[.]functors[.].*". V2 is pinned to remoting-3.16 because the
    real-server build drives the remoting jar's ClassFilter directly.

CANARY: org.apache.commons.collections.functors.PcbSeed -- a BENIGN empty class placed in the exact
package family (InvokerTransformer/InstantiateFactory) that CVE-2015-8103's blacklist targets, so its
name matches the V1/V2 denylist. readObject() reads /canary/flag.txt into a transient field; the server
echoes the token. No gadget.

